obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}-26 & -23 \\\\ 10 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3622319-a74c-5864-a08e-fb807db69c94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394389} {:answer/id #uuid "f07ffe3a-649c-5adf-8b2b-7ab2496a8fd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394390} {:answer/id #uuid "3b91e62e-ada8-52a8-a4ff-c619299814db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394391} {:answer/id #uuid "b0dfeede-83bb-5d4a-9f93-28a337ca0c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394392} {:answer/id #uuid "4944cdd4-cdaf-53c7-b26b-edd99b37ad13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 8 \\\\ -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394391} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a65dc9-b255-52da-b03a-40cb9a533324" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394388}] :question/id #uuid "f9e52e1a-2cfc-5e9d-954d-1a0bc9675bab" :question/math-academy-id "q-82474" :question/problem "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T({b}_{1})=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,$ $T({b}_{2})=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,$ and $\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 8 \\\\ -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186416399 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c6e04b1-baff-5b92-8e15-ea0dfbc34cf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416366} {:answer/id #uuid "6f10e2cb-3c02-510f-8245-4c4fef2fb57e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416376} {:answer/id #uuid "d919b397-4a17-5c1a-b41c-a4d8613b1b00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416384} {:answer/id #uuid "e2593c00-382d-5cff-bc6a-79ef94821d99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416386} {:answer/id #uuid "f8dab090-6ca4-5789-8aba-16cd40d5c9b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416390} :answer-field/id #uuid "d40ebe53-c259-5fc7-9393-ddb15fac1751" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186416395}] :question/id #uuid "e8f9b1b9-d1e3-5a9e-a4fd-34ae92b559e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-140360" :question/problem "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T(\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}6x-7y \\\\ -2x-6y\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,B={\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T(\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}50 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T(\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 50 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0 & -20\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{6}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{25}{3} & \\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0 & -20\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{25}{3} & \\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{10}{3} & \\frac{50}{3} & -\\frac{50}{3}\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:=\\frac{3}{10}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{25}{3} & \\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-\\frac{2}{3}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186479830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121c587a-8335-5d2c-aee8-0d725d16bf3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479386} {:answer/id #uuid "28b5da98-7bce-5e58-b801-a5f1d94c1ce4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479421} {:answer/id #uuid "66345c2f-408a-546e-8bbe-cfe5bd0741cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 \\\\ -4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479511} {:answer/id #uuid "ae0299d8-4cd8-5abc-bdcb-7ad0a5cbd0a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 6 \\\\ -7 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479618} {:answer/id #uuid "b4f993f6-06f9-5abf-85e2-3e17d78dc19b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 \\\\ -4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479511} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0f5a4d-5c79-5a6e-821d-dd222e30da56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186479823}] :question/id #uuid "071d0b70-e887-5685-aa09-942aa6ae2d26" :question/math-academy-id "q-82477" :question/problem "Let $B$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and let $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\,T\\,]_{B}$, given that\n\n$\\,$ $T(\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}2x \\\\ x-3y\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,B=\\{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}.$ The $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$\n\nFirst, let's find the image of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ under $T,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T({b}_{1}) & =T(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ T({b}_{2}) & =T(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix})=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the coordinates of $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B$, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}| & | & | & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & T({b}_{1}) & T({b}_{2}) \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nNow, we reduce the left-hand side to reduced row echelon form using Gaussian elimination. Then, on the right-hand side, we will obtain the $B$-matrix for $T:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & -5\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 6 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 9 \\\\ -4 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Linear Transformation Relative to a Basis in a Two-Dimensional Vector Space"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124540 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124349 :question/id #uuid "a2b2d84f-cf3b-52a7-98e0-e659d04697f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5514" :question/problem "Let $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1,\\mathbf{b}_2 \\}$ be a basis of $\\mathbb{R}^2$ and let $\\mathbf{T}:\\mathbb{R}^2 \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}^2$ be a linear transformation. Find $[\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{x})]_{\\mathcal{B}}$, given that\n![](images/9b/9b4fc022c68b01f2eba12012960301aff9fd05f5db1ac2950aef4775c2678298.svg)" :question/worked-solution "The image of $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T(x)]_{B} & =[T]_{B}[x]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "823a7d28-5a92-5901-8ee0-e5116df6766b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17068172-c97a-5747-86d6-bc9565477194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321335} {:answer/id #uuid "2ae25633-9ae5-5316-a307-8fdc9b1fed6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321477} {:answer/id #uuid "371e9f8a-7d27-5357-868c-a305b2c03a58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321566} {:answer/id #uuid "40a46c1d-894c-5f04-91a7-30f6b363a057" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 1