 | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2} &=-5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n5{c}_{1}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2\\cdot 1+{c}_{2}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dee1b9d5-e9ec-5bfa-a8c6-84defeffa71d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301069}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301069} :answer-field/id #uuid "003a2f30-99f7-56c0-9fca-f8c62ad20cf2" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbd01cb0-acbb-56ba-a897-9b433e0f13b3" 