| {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} \\\\ -2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} &=5 \\\\ -2{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n5{c}_{2}=10\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+2\\cdot 2=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302283 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed8f2501-608e-5490-875c-a171a0633d55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301137} :answer-field/id #uuid "90732163-32b9-5b07-865c-bcdf9a67c138" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301686} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e9eec7a-b969-5197-985a-2bbde2cc2192" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300685} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2a534fc-8516-546e-a281-eef08993f86a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301750} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cddcadf-c0b8-5bcf-b396-4a983942d32d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300096} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae0ffd2c-f554-54ca-a8e2-bbb04592c700" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301791} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b87df21-e2f5-5bf5-bb14-95b10e177a26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299990}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299990} :answer-field/id #uuid "c265bf2a-e7bf-5da3-b27a-a0b097e1e5ad" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301860}] :question/id #uuid "3ba6f2a7-7dbc-5be9-8beb-c38e3acae4d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-326298" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngiven that the general solution to our differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}-{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {c}_{1}-{c}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get\n\n$$\n2{c}_{1}=4\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2+{c}_{2}=4\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "106c801b-9793-5ac4-ba68-8207722b9989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370051} :answer-field/id #uuid "6192aeee-0627-5345-a17b-c332a3aef75d" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370050} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6d09e27-477f-57fe-b56f-5fc94464d73d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370053} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfd819cb-2e5e-5d53-939a-5e2abfa5a4d6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370052} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7da4a3b4-b767-5c03-b93d-72160a95f926" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370055} :answer-field/id #uuid "71a2f86f-7423-5f5e-a912-1cbd2c93a9cd" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370054} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61e44b2f-f15b-5664-94e6-6bdd453a6df7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370057} :answer-field/id #uuid "634d106e-bc4b-5878-9a00-670b61553812" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370056}] :question/id #uuid "feaf5cff-8b17-5206-b24f-3f656646691a" :question/math-academy-id "q-326292" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngiven that the general solution to our differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=1 \\\\ 2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} &=8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get\n\n$$\n3{c}_{1}=9\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n3+{c}_{2}=1\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}\\,+\\,(-2)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}\\,+\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413788 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc789ad9-fd8d-540d-b522-2e14081e3a89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413770} :answer-field/id #uuid "50a25668-c10b-5eab-bdcc-4ddc7f6b1b4e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c786fd8-d7ed-5f2a-9e53-0a7f840fdbdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413755} :answer-field/id #uuid "5506a205-5b30-551f-b363-f141058018cc" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d59ce5ae-84c8-5a2d-a4a1-8bd238cda117" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413762}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413762} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d4861c2-d3fe-5c16-bbc5-4dadf84b619c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413778} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09520544-6bc1-51eb-8597-077df0f8f535" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413746}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413746} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd206b91-8f38-5ab2-9e44-158195118e5a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413782}] :question/id #uuid "216d1aeb-34d0-53e9-bbe2-39e35d3f0d63" :question/math-academy-id "q-326296" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngiven that the general solution to our differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $-2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-5{c}_{1}=-5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n3\\cdot 1+{c}_{2}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413789 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "102c058e-dc31-5c85-9478-992372c3c8ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413747} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f0ddeaa-0a2f-529a-a7bd-3d095a96c1bc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413776} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbaeb046-8870-5540-88a9-d88923b77b06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413764}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413764} :answer-field/id #uuid "81df9d5d-2f2e-5227-b53d-455a1bcfec46" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8084dc72-05d6-52af-90fe-7e244dfcffda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413756}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413756} :answer-field/id #uuid "976e8d31-0eac-5826-97fb-e5a72ed1f999" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e0cddd2-dabf-5ba9-af95-b6ad2b8f31fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413754} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe194b1f-4a94-5286-8851-0626336088fd" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413786}] :question/id #uuid "514febb9-898e-5a8c-8e7f-718f51a9867b" :question/math-academy-id "q-326297" :question/problem "Solve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngiven that the general solution to our differential equation is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nThe solution to the initial value problem is\n\n| $x(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,\\,{e}^{-t}.$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "To find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=2 \\\\ {c}_{1}-2{c}_{2} &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n3{c}_{1}=9\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n3+{c}_{2}=2\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+(-1)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the General Solution"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129312 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128954 :question/id #uuid "226a5f8f-ac26-5f3e-8f8f-f145c314820f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5609" :question/problem "Let $\\lambda_1=3$ and $\\lambda_2=-2$ be eigenvalues of the $2\\times 2$ matrix  $A$ that correspond to eigenvectors \n![](images/be/bea45856123519703211eba01e1c6fe6b3cf8cd045eb7b2ad2a2a3a7cf9adc43.svg) \nGiven that the position of a particle at time $t$ seconds is given by the vector $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ and that $\\mathbf{x}(t)$ is the solution to the initial value problem\n![](images/62/62ced02d9670f7b749e19ea357508aeb57f6b65777d6c2dd5adc4d2e35172688.svg)\nfind the position of the particle after $2$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\color{red}\\lambda_1}, {\\color{blue}\\lambda_2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${\\color{red}\\mathbf{v}_1}$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = c_1{\\color{red}\\mathbf{v}_1} e^{{\\color{red}\\lambda_1} t} + c_2{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2} e^{{\\color{blue}\\lambda_2} t}, \\qquad c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2,$ we substitute $t=0$ into the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}6{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ -2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=-11 \\\\ -2{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n16c_1 = -32\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nc_1=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-2\\cdot(-2) -3c_2 = 1\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nc_2=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution for the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =-2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+1\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $\\mathbf x(2)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3\\cdot 2}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12{e}^{6}+{e}^{-4} \\\\ 4{e}^{6}-3{e}^{-4}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "35a8694d-4fa1-54a6-a492-3025cb627fa1" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cd6362-418e-5da5-9c64-68de1dfef87f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324012} {:answer/id #uuid "58cf8d5a-ede1-5b00-b440-c720f8596f38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324707} {:answer/id #uuid "bfa83116-7539-5ba7-8043-771e084a8e58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325619} {:answer/id #uuid "c24f1fe1-958b-595b-8e52-9ceda5f109a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325639} {:answer/id #uuid "ee604193-7a03-5f77-a6ed-74d0c5cf8685" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325639} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e494f66-b204-5fea-8bf6-9e12133ee3dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326476}] :question/id #uuid "d9d3d68e-7221-5fb6-8c31-50910c28ab47" :question/math-academy-id "q-39240" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} \\\\ -2{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} &=3 \\\\ -2{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n6{c}_{2}=3\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=3\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129726 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "122c29b3-6de6-5b73-ab41-6a3897c547e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4+{e}^{2} \\\\ {e}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324135} {:answer/id #uuid "7429d813-2d31-54f1-905f-a61b12d52b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5+{e}^{10} \\\\ 1+{e}^{10}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324939} {:answer/id #uuid "8ceb37a5-2969-5718-bf6b-1bf1a5c85703" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4+{e}^{5} \\\\ {e}^{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325168} {:answer/id #uuid "9a85e094-300d-540f-b01d-562e2dfb5e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4+{e}^{10} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325287} {:answer/id #uuid "d7fb6670-08cf-5083-ad24-6157376ac93f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4+{e}^{10} \\\\ {e}^{10}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4+{e}^{10} \\\\ {e}^{10}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325851} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b61174c-c8e9-5dfb-88fa-9ac0766af906" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326443}] :question/id #uuid "d1f184ac-fee2-55eb-900b-6eaef0d92cda" :question/math-academy-id "q-39241" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the position of a particle at time $t$ seconds is given by the vector $x(t),$ and that $x(t)$ is the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nfind the position of the particle at $t=5$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ into the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} \\\\ 2{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} &=5 \\\\ 2{c}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=4.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution for the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =4\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $x(5)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(5) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2\\cdot 5} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{10} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4+{e}^{10} \\\\ {e}^{10}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326756 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1def90c1-295c-513f-8d17-08d3eb728d5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6{e}^{28}+18{e}^{-7} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324223} {:answer/id #uuid "9c44ae5b-89ec-5509-b374-71c79cd546e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18{e}^{28}+24{e}^{-7} \\\\ -6{e}^{28}+18{e}^{-7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325296} {:answer/id #uuid "c6f9a8f0-7ca4-532a-8c5c-a15bc32f000b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-18{e}^{7}+24{e}^{-7} \\\\ -18{e}^{7}+18{e}^{-7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325689} {:answer/id #uuid "d23922bc-ad96-548d-bd19-9c0401a8f083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-18{e}^{28}+24{e}^{-7} \\\\ -18{e}^{28}+18{e}^{-7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325797} {:answer/id #uuid "e07bab0e-82d0-59c4-900c-aee316593406" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12{e}^{28}+28{e}^{-7} \\\\ -18{e}^{28}+16{e}^{-7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-18{e}^{28}+24{e}^{-7} \\\\ -18{e}^{28}+18{e}^{-7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325797} :answer-field/id #uuid "92bb4f1b-aee1-5145-b7ea-470f04edbde6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326481}] :question/id #uuid "c2ab3368-1586-5095-a52c-feadd0cc4835" :question/math-academy-id "q-39280" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=4$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the position of a particle at time $t$ seconds is given by the vector $x(t),$ and that $x(t)$ is the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nfind the position of the particle at $t=7$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ into the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2} \\\\ -{c}_{1}+3{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{c}_{1}+4{c}_{2} &=6 \\\\ -{c}_{1}+3{c}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second equation by $-1$ and adding the result to the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n{c}_{2}=6.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-{c}_{1}+4\\cdot 6=6\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=18.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =18\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+6\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $x(7)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(7) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4\\cdot 7}+\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-7} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ -18\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{28}+\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-7} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18{e}^{28}+24{e}^{-7} \\\\ -18{e}^{28}+18{e}^{-7}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371105 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5572763-9798-5541-88d1-7eff664f6124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5{e}^{-9} \\\\ {e}^{-9}+5{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371107} {:answer/id #uuid "3dccc843-2599-507e-a533-65cb44274b4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{-9} \\\\ 5{e}^{-9}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371108} {:answer/id #uuid "09a56494-a89b-5756-a703-dc8bcc76ebfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10{e}^{-9} \\\\ -2{e}^{-9}-5{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371109} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a8714e-2f6c-54c2-9251-8bb23af96e62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{-9} \\\\ 5{e}^{-9}-2{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371110} {:answer/id #uuid "b2e8538d-e4af-5497-94a8-5b4c60e5c5b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5{e}^{-9} \\\\ 5{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371111}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10{e}^{-9} \\\\ -2{e}^{-9}-5{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371109} :answer-field/id #uuid "a24153c5-9dd8-5631-a7a5-5e9a93fac81c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371106}] :question/id #uuid "27ca83bf-1817-5b87-965e-2e220104951a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79783" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the position of a particle at time $t$ seconds is given by the vector $x(t),$ and that $x(t)$ is the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nfind the position of the particle at $t=3$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ into the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-5{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5{c}_{1} &=10 \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=-7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-5{c}_{1}=10\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n-2+{c}_{2}=-7\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-5.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution for the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =-2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+(-5)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $x(3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(3) & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3\\cdot 3}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2\\cdot 3} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-9}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{6} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10{e}^{-9} \\\\ -2{e}^{-9}-5{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "031fcf4c-44d6-5f96-acb1-353d67b1fad7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389610} {:answer/id #uuid "8a74ffc8-d62f-510a-82cc-c909e16d7fcc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389611} {:answer/id #uuid "8513d342-7c71-558c-bb5b-2d0b8669c8c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389612} {:answer/id #uuid "89d6b4d2-63a0-58db-b23d-fe914857704c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389613} {:answer/id #uuid "ede6c55e-98c0-5183-847e-807c623a05f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389612} :answer-field/id #uuid "36a4ed42-4ec3-5cae-83cc-1a4e796d7a8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389609}] :question/id #uuid "d561dbfb-7ee3-58dc-8154-27aa2bc8812a" :question/math-academy-id "q-168916" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2(0)} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} \\\\ 5{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 5{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2} &=8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get\n\n$$\n6{c}_{1}=12\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n2+2{c}_{2}=4\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+1\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389615 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fde92cf-da54-5afe-9f1a-b3d21d6bf290" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-4}+4{e}^{6} \\\\ 5{e}^{-4}-4{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389617} {:answer/id #uuid "87090451-e0b4-56e6-a0c2-708d60d4f12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-4}+3{e}^{6} \\\\ -{e}^{-4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389618} {:answer/id #uuid "306f0ec4-5a23-5893-a77a-0c4ccd9d70a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-4} \\\\ 5{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389619} {:answer/id #uuid "51a41736-479c-5cbe-a6a5-f920a289f460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{-4}+4{e}^{6} \\\\ {e}^{-4}-4{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389620} {:answer/id #uuid "8e43a50c-201c-59de-8f0a-2df24646008e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3{e}^{6} \\\\ -4{e}^{-4}+{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-4}+4{e}^{6} \\\\ 5{e}^{-4}-4{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389617} :answer-field/id #uuid "207eb684-605f-5bc6-8756-8f315ee86796" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389616}] :question/id #uuid "048c4d19-f776-56af-aac6-30cdbc559443" :question/math-academy-id "q-168917" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=-2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the position of a particle at time $t$ seconds is given by the vector $x(t),$ and that $x(t)$ is the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nfind the position of the particle at $t=2$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ into the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2(0)}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3(0)} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 5{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 5{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get\n\n$$\n4{c}_{1}=4\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-1+{c}_{2}=3\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=4.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =1\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}+4\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $x(2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(2) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2(2)}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3(2)} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-4}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{6} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{-4}+4{e}^{6} \\\\ 5{e}^{-4}-4{e}^{6}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393961 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30a1dfc9-55d7-539a-838d-044ac35e80d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-28 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393963} {:answer/id #uuid "83a52428-f1f4-5108-b0a0-b6352996e457" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393964} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0a9834-3295-5cb6-905a-0b4f396a620a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393965} {:answer/id #uuid "97de5ba9-b8b6-5289-83c2-d23ef4668cec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393966} {:answer/id #uuid "c3579650-87ed-5901-a05a-88d7d64bf7c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{8t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393966} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2f43ed9-70b5-571a-9342-1d4d9a3e81be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393962}] :question/id #uuid "cbc7fbb6-5ecf-5e40-98fc-81b2c93a104a" :question/math-academy-id "q-79733" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=4 \\\\ {c}_{1} &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n4\\cdot 3+{c}_{2}=4\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-8.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution for the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+(-8)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24ed8036-d2f0-5678-aded-6e9c044ca85d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413749} {:answer/id #uuid "2867dfa3-059a-58fa-b11f-d0bedd4e7491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413751} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd33a37-99bf-5651-bb5f-06e9f817bff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413758} {:answer/id #uuid "e645af68-19cd-5af5-9c27-6263465a9288" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413766} {:answer/id #uuid "fde1093c-8ee3-592c-af49-4b7e84a1917a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413771} :answer-field/id #uuid "5eb02b51-88b6-54c6-8e3a-87a5f60dbdfd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413775}] :question/id #uuid "05d28970-6cfe-5fc6-bc98-6f13f1fbcff5" :question/math-academy-id "q-39270" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{c}_{2} \\\\ 7{c}_{1}-{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{c}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 7{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} &=14.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n7{c}_{1}-0=14\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution for the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+0\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413791 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "161a2113-6f77-577f-b8dd-070e7d29117d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10{e}^{9}-4{e}^{-6} \\\\ -10{e}^{9}+2{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413748} {:answer/id #uuid "579b934f-3562-585a-9c58-868d0ac299b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{9}+12{e}^{-6} \\\\ 10{e}^{9}-6{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413752} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec3aa86-7c65-5073-99dc-9b9434d81635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2{e}^{9}+{e}^{-6} \\\\ -{e}^{9}-{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413759} {:answer/id #uuid "bcad915f-ea19-5199-a4f9-a7af8a70c018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}512{e}^{-6} \\\\ 5{e}^{9}-2{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413761} {:answer/id #uuid "fbd36ee8-9de1-5381-988c-ad17c88ac46f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{9} \\\\ 5{e}^{9}+6{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413769}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{9}+12{e}^{-6} \\\\ 10{e}^{9}-6{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413752} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4863853-4c96-5cb6-a514-351184df6735" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413785}] :question/id #uuid "c7ea76f4-22db-56a5-acbc-fee92d706737" :question/math-academy-id "q-79729" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nGiven that the position of a particle at time $t$ seconds is given by the vector $x(t),$ and that $x(t)$ is the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nfind the position of the particle at $t=3$ seconds." :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=3$ into the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{c}_{1}-2{c}_{2} &=2 \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get\n\n$$\n-{c}_{2}=6\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-6.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}+(-6)=4\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=10.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =10\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+(-6)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate $x(3)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(3) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3\\cdot 3}+\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2\\cdot 3} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{9}+\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-6} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10{e}^{9}+12{e}^{-6} \\\\ 10{e}^{9}-6{e}^{-6}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186493908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0960efec-d285-5cdd-9e4c-60cdf590887c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}30 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493406} {:answer/id #uuid "75efba6a-e437-5328-8072-189d93667b50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}35 \\\\ 26\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-28 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493567} {:answer/id #uuid "a00c0b88-91a7-5321-9fb1-4c0eb83e8718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}30 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-28 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493644} {:answer/id #uuid "baae230c-b658-5758-b99c-87c465155740" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493696} {:answer/id #uuid "eb9a0dee-ec6c-54ab-9bd5-bc8eda85ad1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 30\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}30 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-28 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493644} :answer-field/id #uuid "8bc94f58-c888-5f48-8bc9-61a9a2954b43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493845}] :question/id #uuid "2dd7bee1-71b3-5685-9b9f-df2041d5d283" :question/math-academy-id "q-79732" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1$ corresponding to the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ respectively, where\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSolve the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1},{\\lambda }_{2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution to our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$, we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}5{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=2 \\\\ {c}_{1} &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=6.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n5\\cdot 6+{c}_{2}=2\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-28.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the solution for the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =6\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+(-28)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}30 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-28 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem Given the Eigenvectors and Eigenvalues of the Corresponding Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129313 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186128953 :question/id #uuid "d2768264-6d1a-5e62-9af4-025c877e138b" :question/math-academy-id "e-5608" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n![](images/8f/8fdedaad6e0d10a2bfab94f4266830a5efefbe2997d05455fecb35cbf7cefb43.svg)\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_1=2$ and $\\lambda_2=-3.$*" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)$ for the given system\n![](images/7a/7a07096a35f46528c18bdce5e711a5e813ac1923342e06cbff3f3c6b3215ae64.svg)\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n\\lambda_1= 2\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\lambda_2= -3.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For $\\lambda_1 =2,$ we get \n![](images/28/284acfc8cb4726bec4f4e805a8be0c037b38a0b9af287a27a4c7f5a2f1679d60.svg)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/b3/b33588ca4b487e1de13aac19bdfc5347751dbe95a9f93c27729d7da54ab02e06.svg)\n\n- For $\\lambda_2 =-3,$ we get \n![](images/1c/1c6b0e7303099895b50f884468ba6bfb7830ec88bbaea17dbc322a5a70eeea4c.svg)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](images/bb/bb4d152439d5a97dfda5196a24752e2048fb421a8cfac5c67ffbab512115d0c8.svg)\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the values of $c_1$ and $c_2,$ we substitute $t=0$ in the general solution and use the initial values:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+6{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}+6{c}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{c}_{2}=-5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $c_2 = -1$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-1=5\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =6\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "833d0ec0-d895-5d66-b2ad-d058858caf9e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129582 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "006c6611-e018-504a-a01c-32aef354674d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299933} {:answer/id #uuid "4867cad9-c101-5cc1-9ce1-f22a654e0225" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300328} {:answer/id #uuid "89b4be77-7a0c-52fe-bdfe-13c390e402fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300658} {:answer/id #uuid "bead334f-835b-513e-937d-1e09bd4a9b13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300913} {:answer/id #uuid "cd7d33b5-0d60-5b9d-afdb-fc4a819ff4e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300913} :answer-field/id #uuid "1132d972-9068-5f5b-bea7-ae90f79c57d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301282}] :question/id #uuid "c2f46aeb-4fa8-5261-bc96-7f74682a5de2" :question/math-academy-id "q-324462" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=4{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- Since $A$ is upper-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=4\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=4,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4(0)}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\ 5{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ 5{c}_{2} &=10.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${c}_{2}=2.$ Substituting into the first equation, we obtain ${c}_{1}=1.$ \n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129583 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab7e0ce9-0b69-5dd3-a368-3cc1da284569" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370044} {:answer/id #uuid "f6e34118-c9d0-5956-a8ce-2eaaecfc99ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+5\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370045} {:answer/id #uuid "a42a97c5-ccd6-5b4d-9a83-19aeeb71c358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370046} {:answer/id #uuid "d56b7809-8b90-5f3f-871c-86a6b90b4486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370047} {:answer/id #uuid "a923eb6b-6333-5907-be70-a7184211d7c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=5\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370044} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9a329d6-e958-5db1-9f6a-f6e439f8337a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370043}] :question/id #uuid "49d0e43c-ac04-5d4e-a46f-7b5d2747eccc" :question/math-academy-id "q-324500" :question/problem "Find the solution to the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=3.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=3.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1}-{c}_{2} &=9 \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=6.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{c}_{1}=15\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{1}=5$ into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5+{c}_{2}=6\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =5\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302319 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3de5b098-ae89-5d21-8244-c5229e3ad0eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=8\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300264} {:answer/id #uuid "3ea18dd7-af5c-58e0-aeda-7636bb0039ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}-8\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300268} {:answer/id #uuid "7515dfea-02d5-5ad3-8e62-16898787c7fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+8\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300543} {:answer/id #uuid "7b22658b-9503-590b-a9e5-d337f57f77db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-4\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300574} {:answer/id #uuid "7b51fd6c-e30a-512e-873f-f9aa4798c054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-8\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-8\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300575} :answer-field/id #uuid "df635750-1749-5071-949b-9e2eea60806f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301936}] :question/id #uuid "323aa95a-cd97-5a1e-8432-085c87b86469" :question/math-academy-id "q-327132" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=5{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- Since $A$ is upper-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=5,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ {c}_{2} &=3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${c}_{2}=3.$ Substituting into the first equation, we obtain ${c}_{1}=-8.$ \n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =-8\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0946d515-d77d-5152-a7ec-18d350713625" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299978} {:answer/id #uuid "5194cb40-978f-55a6-b03d-2caa7acc356d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300385} {:answer/id #uuid "5c323eb2-48f1-5247-958f-56f399c1344f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300438} {:answer/id #uuid "9a73d9ed-9176-57ad-ad65-61e54f207ea5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+4\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300738} {:answer/id #uuid "a64f3f3d-d708-5e0a-b529-d766dc084e75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=2\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}-4\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300800}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300385} :answer-field/id #uuid "13ebfe34-7b6d-5da2-a3b2-14dbc0b0f46c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301291}] :question/id #uuid "c7343f41-95b5-5176-9f70-e4d55b426d92" :question/math-academy-id "q-327160" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-4{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1/4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2(0)} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ 4{c}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 4{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{c}_{1}=-3\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{1}=-1$ into the first equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1+{c}_{2}=2\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-2t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370065 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b9bda6e-7e9f-5f46-a9ff-034b8fce5b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=37\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}-14\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370067} {:answer/id #uuid "45848a5f-be44-5690-ada7-4e4b5a8d8ebc" :answer/type {:db/ident :a