_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3/2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{1}+2{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2} &=5 \\\\ {c}_{1}+2{c}_{2} &=9.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{c}_{2}=14\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{2}=-14$ into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1}-2(-14)=9\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=37.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =37\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-t}-14\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390777 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8b0460a-d0ad-5d76-b63d-e1be79a2bf53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-\\frac{3}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\frac{9}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390779} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a14dfc-50da-56c0-9bcf-ac663a34125d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-\\frac{7}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}+\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390780} {:answer/id #uuid "1dbcec44-0f8c-57c6-8f12-e880f0d06cfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{3}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{9}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390781} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1d5dc2-3635-56a3-a363-0ad6d716256c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390782} {:answer/id #uuid "a1dd86f6-75a2-50a1-af44-6ffa5adbb75f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{7}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}-\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}