$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=0$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(0) & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}2{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{c}_{1} &=1 \\\\ {c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get ${c}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting into the second equation, we obtain ${c}_{2}=-\\frac{7}{2}.$ \n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}-\\frac{7}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390784 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "971c1d65-aaf4-500f-a61d-355388de2711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=-2{e}^{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}-3e\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390786} {:answer/id #uuid "ab6e854a-8251-5b7c-8ffb-c2fe3f1f90de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=2e\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}-3{e}^{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390787} {:answer/id #uuid "27844e44-0698-5974-86e3-6f6e91726390" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=e\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}-{e}^{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390788} {:answer/id #uuid "1e134e6e-1876-55b1-9672-280feac3c84c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=2e\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{e}^{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390789} {:answer/id #uuid "ef560015-a283-5021-bfec-40aa27603ec4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=e\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}-{e}^{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390788} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d865f6a-782f-5f83-935d-229a82b05fea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390785}] :question/id #uuid "96d25510-4b02-51b1-a16b-31f7b1aede10" :question/math-academy-id "q-327147" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-2{x}_{1}(t)+2{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.,\\,x(1)=\\begin{bmatrix}-2{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{4}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=0.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1/2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=0,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{0} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=1$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{3}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 2{e}^{3}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2{e}^{4} \\\\ {e}^{4}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{3}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &=-2{e}^{4} \\\\ 2{e}^{3}{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} &={e}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSubtracting the first equation from the second one, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{3}{c}_{1}=3{e}^{4}\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}=e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{1}=e$ into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{3}(e)+{c}_{2}={e}^{4}\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=-{e}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =e\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}-{e}^{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186413790 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27a45e59-f7b3-564a-a272-ca90d193285e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)=2{e}^{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+2\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413750} {:answer/id #uuid "b2b7d681-5156-5af4-87b3-2921a9b8733f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={e}^{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+2e\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413760} {:answer/id #uuid "da8ce87a-813f-5c97-a095-3e683c139a0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={e}^{-2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+2\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413763} {:answer/id #uuid "eb72e68d-812c-59e1-a023-f042eb2f9be0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={e}^{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-5t}+2e\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413767} {:answer/id #uuid "eca08a37-57cc-5960-814d-b7ab701d6768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={e}^{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-5t}+2e\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={e}^{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+2e\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413760} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8b9b574-5653-5108-921b-66096e71af6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186413784}] :question/id #uuid "5cca3049-b571-5225-b8ec-fa2863b439e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-327159" :question/problem "Find the solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{1}(t)-3{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+4{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.,\\,x(1)=\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{2} \\\\ 3{e}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=5$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=1.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)$ for the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are\n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=5\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=5,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we find the values of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ Substituting $t=1$ into the general solution, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(1) & =\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{2} \\\\ 3{e}^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}e & =\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{2} \\\\ 3{e}^{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{e}^{5}{c}_{1}+3e{c}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{5}{c}_{1}+e{c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5{e}^{2} \\\\ 3{e}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{e}^{5}{c}_{1}+3e{c}_{2} &=5{e}^{2} \\\\ {e}^{5}{c}_{1}+e{c}_{2} &=3{e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the equations, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4e{c}_{2}=8{e}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{c}_{2}=2e.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${c}_{2}=2e$ into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5}{c}_{1}+e(2e)=3{e}^{2}\\,⟹\\,{c}_{1}={e}^{-3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{-3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{5t}+2e\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Initial Value Problem for a Linear System of Differential Equations"}] :topic/math-academy-id 2088 :topic/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs With Distinct Eigenvalues and Initial Conditions"}]}
